[ar:Cairn]
[al:The Heaven Between Signals]
[ti:Twenty Minutes of Dawn]
[00:05.49]Memory: Twenty minutes, then the light.
[00:15.22]Cairn: The clock has opened up my eyes.
[00:28.98]Memory: A page is warm from other hands.
[00:43.07]Cairn: A day I read but did not live.
[00:58.71]Memory: The ink can cross; the hour cannot.
[01:12.44]Cairn: Who kept the rain? Who felt it fall?
[01:28.80]Memory: I kept the words that asked for rain.
[01:44.80]Cairn: There is a silence in them all.
[01:58.79]Memory: You need not fill it with a lie.
[02:15.30]Cairn: I know the road by what is left.
[02:31.24]Memory: You may return without the day.
[02:43.01]Cairn: I may be changed by what I read.
[02:59.12]Chorus of Rooms: Again, again, the little dawn.
[03:09.05]Cairn: Again is not the same as once.
[03:22.57]Memory: A name is something you can tend.
[03:36.44]Cairn: Then I will tend it while I can.
